{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522504-seven-planetary-courts-homebrew","id":1522504,"title":"Seven Planetary Courts (Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-13T00:51:52-07:00","id":1522504,"title":"Seven Planetary Courts (Homebrew)","content":"Hey everyone! After discussion in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1451037-thrice-great-in-2e\">this thread</a> I've decided to write out the Mystery behind Thrice-Great in more detail for my own games; after some thoughts I've decided to share it, both to get some feedback and new ideas and for somebody else to use it if they wish to.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\"><b>Seven Planetary Courts</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Mystery of <i>Henads</i></span><br /> Great and ancient Mystery of Shadow Realm which was focus for Awakened - especially Thrice-Great Legacy who made that Mystery their focus and primary source of mystical might - over untold millennia, Seven Planetary Courts are spirit courts of seven &quot;planets&quot; of Solar System - in Ptolemaic, geocentric system. Even though Awakened magic and Sleeper science disproved that system untold ages ago, the Mystery itself remains.<br /> <br /> Those spirits, called <i>henads</i> by Indo-European Awakened or <i>mulhithim</i> by Uratha, differ from their Earthbound cousins. For any mage who did not ever met a <i>henad</i> of particular planetary court before, they count as Mystery with Opacity (or Keys, if using Mysteries as Investigations) of (3 + their Rank); until Mage hasn't successfully learned their Mystery (and by extension - Mystery of their court), they Withstand attempts to use Knowing spells (of <b>all</b> Arcana) on them with (3 + their Rank) and <i>double</i> their Rank for Spirit spells meant to affect them. While <i>henads</i> know First Tongue and speak it normally, they often have weird accents and inflexions which make it harder to understand them for those who only spoke to earthbound spirits before, imposing -3 penalty on any social rolls with them.<br /> <br /> But it's not their alien Supernal symbolism which is the main Obsession of Awakened all over the world, but unique, strange Resonance-signatures they have. Sleepers know other planets to be dead, lifeless balls of rock or gas giants; one would expect their spirits to be the same - spirits of cold, dark matter endlessly circling the distant sun. But they anything but; every planetary court has it's unique symbolism and resonances, including very <i>human</i> concepts such as desires, emotions or ethical principles. The chicken-and-egg debate over source of such Resonance-concepts is going for several millennia now with end nowhere in sight; while most Diamond and Seer mages think this to be result of Supernal over-symbol influences (with many mages arguing that planets themselves may be connected to hypothetical Celestial Ladder and it's shattering during the Fall), Free Council mages think that influence of humanity is more far-reaching than anyone have thought, somehow influencing distant Shadows.<br /> <br /> No matter the reason, <i>henads</i> themselves are powerful, if alien, allies to Awakened when called upon and properly bargained with. They are able to grant Patron Yantras with bonus equal to their (Rank/2, round up), linked to concepts of their planetary courts; their very presence counts as Environment Yantra for such spells. They are able to aid and empower acts of ritual magic, acting as Sleepwalkers or even fully Awakened for such spells. While they lack knowledge of Arcana themselves, not being Supernal Entities (though sometimes they act like they are distant cousins of them), many of them know ancient secrets, including Rotes and magical techniques lost to time. And of course, there are their Influences, which can be used for wide range of tasks.<br /> <br /> Their requests, however, are as alien as <i>henads</i> themselves; not having spheres of influence in terrestrial Shadow, many of them are interested in bizarre quests in it nonetheless - sometimes destructive, sometimes restorative, but always strange. A lot of <i>henads</i> seem to be interested in human worship; given that they are curiously similar to likes of many ancient pagan gods, this raises questions about genesis of many Sleeper religions. Powerful and prepared Awakened can try to defy them and wrestle and beat them into submission instead, but their Mystery is powerful one; <i>henads</i> wield many strange and terrifying Numina, some of which seem to be <i>especially</i> effective against Supernal magic, and a lot of too hubristic mages have met their end this way.<br /> <br /> The Mystery becomes even more perplexing when most knowledgeable Awakened start to consider effects of planetary courts on Earth as a whole. While choirs of Warden Moon prohibit the direct entry to their celestial cousins (strangely, all <i>henads</i> coming to Earth uninvited and on their own are full of hate and wish to cause as much suffering and destruction as possible), mages know that astrology, while being thought as a fake pseudoscience by contemporary Sleepers, has a kernel of truth (and Truth) in it. Influence of distant planets does manifest itself in Earth's Shadow, creating tidal waves of certain Resonances and affecting related choirs - and thus affecting material realm indirectly. Those &quot;stellar winds&quot; are deep, ancient and elusive Mystery, especially by the fact they are <i>slow</i>, subtly affecting the Earth over course of centuries and sometimes even millennia, making their study a multi-generational effort for entire Legacies to focus upon.<br /> <br /> The lesser, but still curious, Mystery is connecting alchemy and astrology. There are seven well-known planetary courts and seven Perfected metals - and they resonate with each other. When magical tool made out of Perfected metal is used as Yantra in summoning a henad of corresponding planetary court, spell gains one free Reach. The reason for this is anyone's guess, though.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Known Planetary Courts</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Luna/Moon</span><br /> Physically closest to the Earth, <i>Lunes</i> are lunar spirits most familiar and known to Awakened; they are also serve as messengers and heralds from Mother Luna to her earthbound children, Uratha. There are five different &quot;castes&quot; of Lunes roughly corresponding to different moon phases, but Lunes overall are capricious and shapeshifting beings linked to concepts of transformation and madness. They favor Acanthus mages, especially those privy to shapeshifting magic and oracular madness.<br /> <br /> Curiously, they are also bound to protect the Earth Shadow from invasions from other planetary courts and void spirits, and they often corral and command Uratha and sometimes even mages to act in protection of Shadow from such intruders. Fortunately for mages who want to communicate with <i>henads</i> and study them, they rarely react to a quick summoning, but any Awakened trying to bind the <i>henad</i> more permanently will quickly become object of their attention and anger; the more powerful <i>henad</i> in question is, the more deadly such attention will be.<br /> <br /> Lunes are resonating with lunargent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Sun</span><br /> Spiritual children of the Sun itself, <i>Helions</i> are rarely seen in the Shadow Realm - but still much more common than other <i>henads</i>. They are powerful, prideful beings linked to concepts of wrath, justice, revelation and rejection of lies and darkness; they often manifest as blazing fireballs, geometric forms of pure light, or even armed humanoid angel-like figures. They favor Obrimos mages calling them, especially those who fight lies and demand justice - no matter what kind of justice it is - but demand respect (even obeisance) and fealty. Helions grant raw power of revelation and truth, but demand that mages use it fully, without restrictions or holdbacks.<br /> <br /> Helions are resonating with orichalcum.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Mercury</span><br /> The most guile and intelligent of <i>henads</i>, angels of Mercury are ones most interested in Awakened themselves. They are smart, inquisitive beings linked to concepts of intellect, communication, uncovering secrets, trade and theft; they often manifest as lightning-quick shapes constantly on the edge of vision, or even borrow the image from mind of summoner. It was they who helped to create hermeticism as philosophy of thought, and they are <i>henads</i> most mages seek to summon and deal with. They favor all Awakened regardless of Path, but those who summon them have to embrace their Obsessions. Mercury <i>henads</i> hold a lot of secrets traded from Awakened all over the history, and rumors have it that they hold even greater secrets of their own well-hidden under the surface of Mercury.<br /> <br /> Mercury <i>henads</i> are resonating with hermium.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Venus</span><br /> The most human-like <i>henads</i> (thus fueling Free Council theories on Mystery's source), angels of Venus are desire personified. They are seductive, charming beings liked to concepts of desire, inspiration, fertility, joy and mirth; they take beautiful, healthy and appealing forms to cajole and trick Awakened into summoning them. They favor Thyrsus mages, especially those focused on nurturing, protecting and inspiring life itself. Venus <i>henads</i> hold many secrets of healing and inspiration, and able to raise individual to height of his inner potential.<br /> <br /> Venus <i>henads</i> are resonating with brontium.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Mars</span><br /> The most aggressive and dangerous <i>henads</i>, angels of Mars seek to destroy all other planets for the sake of conflict itself. They are warlike, hostile beings linked to concepts of raw emotions (especially anger), warfare, conflicts and violence; but Mars <i>henads</i> also resonate with concepts of boldness, determination and even heroism. They often take forms of red and brown dust and shining tied into ragged, storm-like form ready to unleash power on offender. They favor Mastigos mages, especially those who wield emotions as weapons against other. Mars <i>henads</i> will gladly join Awakened conflicts, but price would be that they will do anything to make them as meaningless and destructive as possible.<br /> <br /> Mars <i>henads</i> are resonating with siderite.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Jupiter</span><br /> <i>Henads</i> of most massive planet (except for the Sun itself), angels of Jupiter see themselves as rightful rulers of all planets - and heirs to the Sun itself. They are ambitious, power-hungry beings linked to concepts of leadership, power, nobility, growth and expansion. They often take massive, powerful, thunderous forms, often vaguely human-like, but sometimes just swirls of wind and force. Like Warden Moon is protector of Earth, Jupiter <i>henads</i> spread their influence all over the Solar System, capturing void spirits in gravity traps and absorbing them and their power. They favor Obrimos mages calling them, but especially those who reach for power and are willing to pay any cost for it.<br /> <br /> Jupiter <i>henads</i> are resonating with kassiterum.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Saturn</span><br /> The most distant <i>henads</i>, angels of Saturn rarely make their way to the Earth on their own; thus most information about them is gained by Awakened through summons and study of stellar winds. They are broody, melancholic beings liked to concepts of obstruction and distress; they command depression and sorrow, and inflict death, sickness leading to endings. They are not malevolent, though; Saturn <i>henads</i> also resonate with <i>overcoming</i> those obstructions to become better. They often look like multicolored, reflective shadows of red and orange hue, constantly fading until they wither away at the end of summoning. They favor Moros mages, especially those who developed a more positive, outward personality after paying with Leaden Coin. They also hold keys to sealing away powerful entities, and experienced Thrice-Great suspect that many such entities are lying, chained and bound, on moons of Saturn.<br /> <br /> Saturn <i>henads</i> resonate with apeiron.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Distant Planets</span><br /> Traditional Hermeticism knows seven planetary bodies; but as Sleeper science has proved, there are more of them. Awakened hold great powers of Arcana, allowing them to know easily there are more than seven major planetary bodies. This is a flexpoint at your table; there are three major possibilities to explore:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Hidden Influences</span><br /> Of course, Awakened Hermetics knew about Uranus, Neptune and Kuiper belt objects; Forces Arcanum is better than any telescope, allowing to focus distant light and explore the night sky. But since contemporary Sleepers were unable to gaze upon those bodies, they never understood obscure references to those distant bodies in Awakened notes and grimoires; desire to keep the Veil stifled the progress. Only now modern occultists have the chance to update old doctrines and fully understand the astrological influences previously only understood by their Awakened mentors.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fractured Courts</span><br /> There are no great <i>henad</i> courts of planetary bodies beyond Saturn. The Mystery ends there; only dispersed Essence-starved spirits of cold winds persist in the clouds of Uranus and Neptune, and Kuiper Belt objects only hold a few void spirits clinging to barren surfaces. While Libertines theorize that spiritual influence of humanity ends near the Saturn orbit, Diamond mages whisper about broken parts of Celestial Ladder falling into the Abyss, stripping symbolism and meaning from those <i>henads</i> stuck in the middle. Some of them even think that Uranus and Neptune are creation of Exarchs, created to destroy the very possibility of rebuilding Celestial Ladder again.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Seed of Possibility</span><br /> In this variant, Mystery ends with Saturn, but not completely. While Uranus does not have it's own formed <i>henads</i> yet, it has a lot more activity than Neptune or Kuiper Belt objects. Various Resonances appear and disappear, as if Shadow of distant planet is itself in the flux. In this variant, planetary court of Uranus is <i>forming;</i> process is astronomically slow and may take centuries or even millennia, but eventually a new type of <i>henad</i> will arise, and perhaps even eighth Perfected metal will appear, linking new planet correspondence to Supernal.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Where is Gaia?</span><br /> Two <i>Ilusahim</i>, Helios and Luna, rule over the Earth's Shadow from above; their existence is known, if arcane, occult fact shared by Awakened and Uratha alike. Existence of <i>Ilusahim</i> of other planets in solar system is implication born from fact that <i>henads</i> and planetary courts exist; it seems obvious that those courts have their overspirits.<br /> <br /> But Earth itself is a spiritual paradox in this regard. Compared to the universe above and beyond, terrestrial Shadow is place of incredible diversity; thousands of different <i>umia</i> exist in Earth's Shadow, with many of them having their own <i>Ilusah</i> or even, possibly, <i>Ilusahim</i> ruling over them. But this begs two questions: is there a planetary court of Earth? And where is Gaia?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><i>Henads</i> of Earth</span><br /> There are two major possibilities for planetary court of Earth which could be explored in your games:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><i>Henads</i> of Earth exist, but Gaia is nowhere to be found.</b> In this variant, Earth is like all other planets; there is a court of planetary spirits of Earth travelling across the void, born out of reflected sunlight; they may protect the Earth from invading void, like Warden Moon does, or they can invade other planets in attempt to seed life there. They can even be hinted to be the ultimate reason other planetary courts exist, giving more credit to Free Council theories. From their existence, Gaia's existence is implied, but this <i>Ilusahim</i>, probably more powerful than Helios or Luna, is still nowhere to be found - which maybe it's own desire.</li> <li><b><i>Henads</i> of Earth do not exist, because Earth is too diverse.</b> There is just no &quot;unifying&quot; symbolism in Earth's shadow - it's too diverse, too vibrant, too ever-changing. It's also cracking with power, with it's own <i>Ilusah</i> and maybe <i>Ilusahim</i> rivaling power of other planetary overspirits. Gaia's existence cannot be implied from these observations, and perhaps pressure of Helios in Earth's Shadow is more sinister than it looks like, preventing court of planetary spirits from <i>forming</i> - and playing their role in conquering the void.</li> </ol><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Does Gaia exist?</span><br /> \u2026this is not very important for average Mage game. Even if it does exist, it's at least Rank 8 (probably more!), standing equal to Luna and Helios, and if such entity wishes to remain unnoticed, nobody except archmages and Ascended Beings can do anything about it. So mere <i>fact</i> is not important enough; the <i>question</i> is much more interesting. Mages and archmages obsessed with that Mystery can go on to grand and dangerous adventures, trying to find Gaia - or even <i>create her</i>, if she does not exist yet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Void and Stars Themselves</span><br /> If <i>henads</i> of distant stars exist, no mage was able to summon them and tell the tale. Perhaps more conservative Thrice-Great are right, and stars are resonant with Supernal itself, while yawning void beyond Solar System is beginning of the Abyss, eating up summoning spells. Or maybe there <i>are</i> such henads, but they are not able to cross the unimaginable distances without becoming void spirits themselves, being forced to subsist on Essence of nothingness - and Awakened magic is not able to create a bridge to them. Strands of sympathy start to break down after heliopause; while distance is Lie, nothing <i>here</i> seems to be really connected, Space-wise, to <i>there</i>. Of course, Forces magic allows to create vessels moving close to speed of light, but so far, mages attempting such expeditions have failed in their attempts, being forced to return or disappearing in the endless expanse of empty space and hungry void.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, void spirits certainly <b>do</b> exist - and their alien, distorted natures give more arguments to those linking those beings to Abyss. While they are certainly not Gulmoth, they share many properties with beings from the Void. They are hungry for Essence. They distort natural laws wherever they appear. They are <i>alien</i>, unlike known <i>henads</i>, barely able to speak First Tongue and be understood. And they wish to <i>invade,</i> trying to create beachheads and strongholds to call more of their own and feast upon reality itself. Because of that, in most Consilia, summoning void spirits is forbidden. Even though Awakened magic is able to feed them and protect world from their influence, doing that invites conflict with Lunes and Uratha. Mages being mages, many ignore that rule to their own peril, quickly finding out that while void spirits are alien beings, they are far from being defenseless.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T04:10:11-07:00","id":1522506,"title":"","content":"I too tried to figure out how to bridge Uratha and Thrice-Great perspectives on Henads. I wondered if the Mages don't actively cultivate desired resonances in contacted Spirits, by feeding them the right essence and making agreements that reinforce their desired symbolism. All that to stop them from being hostile forces and to put them in sync with the hypothetical, pre-Fall paradigm. That would raise a chicken and egg question: Did the Hermetic influences come first, or did the Thrice-Great efforts did?<br /> <br /> This is also why I think Uranus and Neptune would be extremely divisive among the Legacy, even to the point of conflict. Are those two planets even &quot;meant&quot; to exist, and if so, what association to cultivate in them? Should Uranus be granted domain over stillness and preservation befitting its icy nature, or should it be rebellion and deviance representing its wild axial tilt? I imagine arguments like that being common, with a third party shouting that the Planets should develop without interference, and a fourth screaming that all of that is courting the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T08:55:40-07:00","id":1522513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522504-seven-planetary-courts-homebrew?p=1522506#post1522506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too tried to figure out how to bridge Uratha and Thrice-Great perspectives on Henads. I wondered if the Mages don't actively cultivate desired resonances in contacted Spirits, by feeding them the right essence and making agreements that reinforce their desired symbolism. All that to stop them from being hostile forces and to put them in sync with the hypothetical, pre-Fall paradigm. That would raise a chicken and egg question: Did the Hermetic influences come first, or did the Thrice-Great efforts did?<br /> <br /> This is also why I think Uranus and Neptune would be extremely divisive among the Legacy, even to the point of conflict. Are those two planets even &quot;meant&quot; to exist, and if so, what association to cultivate in them? Should Uranus be granted domain over stillness and preservation befitting its icy nature, or should it be rebellion and deviance representing its wild axial tilt? I imagine arguments like that being common, with a third party shouting that the Planets should develop without interference, and a fourth screaming that all of that is courting the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Hermetic Kabbalah, the archangel of Uranus is Uriel, whose domains are Wisdom and alchemy, and whose element is Earth. It probably means he would favor the Moros who invest their leaden coin wisely. Builders, alchemists, medics, those that build civilization, and those that pursue the path of Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Hermetic Kabbalah could be used as a reference point, the henads of Mercury presenting as an inference framework to understand and aid in parsing the Mysteries of the courts, which could explain why the Thrice Great favor that methodology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-13-2023, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T19:06:36-07:00","id":1522549,"title":"","content":"Now I want to see a Hive-Claimed mage rolling with the Essences of all the henads, now Obsessed with searching out and devouring/integrating the other planets\u2019 spirits too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T20:00:07-07:00","id":1522551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522504-seven-planetary-courts-homebrew?p=1522549#post1522549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I want to see a Hive-Claimed mage rolling with the Essences of all the henads, now Obsessed with searching out and devouring/integrating the other planets\u2019 spirits too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I can't help but see that as Spiral's backstory, failing a major trial and falling so far from grace that her soul was wiped clean of the Thrice Great Legacy. Now rather than incorporating elements of the courts as the pathway to the Imperial Mysteries and Omens that would lead to transforming into a new Celestial Ladder, she seeks to integrate spirits with humans, an echo of long lost purpose, warped by the ethos of the Silver Ladder to raise people up to higher rungs of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T20:53:17-07:00","id":1522554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522504-seven-planetary-courts-homebrew?p=1522551#post1522551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I can't help but see that as Spiral's backstory, failing a major trial and falling so far from grace that her soul was wiped clean of the Thrice Great Legacy. Now rather than incorporating elements of the courts as the pathway to the Imperial Mysteries and Omens that would lead to transforming into a new Celestial Ladder, she seeks to integrate spirits with humans, an echo of long lost purpose, warped by the ethos of the Silver Ladder to raise people up to higher rungs of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1350475-a-present-for-merry-wolfenoot?p=1357051#post1357051\">Hive-Claimed sorcerers</a>, but yeah Spiral must've been lodged in my subconscious and waiting for the moment to bubble up like today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a